    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense pivots around **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** today, who remains the cornerstone of the lineup with a stellar 72.41 efficiency score. Facing Gore (L), **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** enjoys a massive 7% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage, and batting in the #3 hole ensures he maintains the high-leverage plate appearances required to drive our RBI and HR totals. While the rest of the roster faces a difficult slate against efficient arms, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**\u2019s ability to punish southpaws in a favorable park environment makes him the only \"Strong\" play on the board today. \n\nOur most challenging decision occurred at the middle infield spots, where **Nasim Nunez** managed to clear the 40-point floor with a 43.24 score, narrowly edging out **Curtis Mead**. While **Curtis Mead** carries a respectable profile, the optimizer relegated him to the bench due to the oppressive 2.84 xERA of the opposing pitcher and a negative 10% platoon adjustment. **Nasim Nunez** earns the start primarily through his switch-hitting flexibility, which mitigates some of the risk posed by S\u00e1nchez, C, though his 43.24 score is undeniably marginal. We are essentially betting on **Nasim Nunez** to utilize his elite speed\u2014our primary scarcity target\u2014to manufacture value on the basepaths, as he is significantly constrained by an opposing catcher with a 1.86s pop time and a suboptimal spot in the #7 hole.\n\nLooking ahead, the roster remains thin due to the ongoing absences of **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, who are either inactive or on the IL, leaving us without our typical offensive engine. We are proceeding cautiously, prioritizing the preservation of our game caps; players like **Curtis Mead** and our deeper reserves were correctly benched as they failed to cross the 40-point threshold against high-quality pitching. With **Nasim Nunez** carrying the load alongside **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, today is a defensive-minded effort to stabilize our category standings until our core contributors return to the active lineup.",
